   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "widgets_values": [
    "HaDeS MOSS Suite - LoRA Surgery (advanced)\n\nBulle d'Encre = SFT with 30% of Base in layers 24-29 + Turbo 8-steps v1.0 x0.5 + a style LoRA x0.8.\nExtracting it gives style and half a turbo in one LoRA; this workflow takes the turbo out again.\n\n1. (muted) LoRA Extractor: Bulle d'Encre minus its rebuilt base, rank 64 (about 100 s, 252 MB).\n2. (muted) LoRA Merger with a negative weight: extracted x1.0 + Turbo v1.0 x-0.30 = the style alone.\n   Why -0.30 and not the recipe's -0.5: the extracted LoRA carries only about two thirds of the half turbo\n   (rank 64 and the bf16 bake lose some), measured on the weights. -0.5 leaves a negative turbo, and\n   at 15 steps the images come out dark and muddy; -0.30 renders like the original style LoRA.\n3. The style on its base with the full turbo (Multi-LoRA, switch it on once bulle_style exists):\n   8 steps, CFG 1, euler / simple, under 4 s. For the style without turbo, switch the turbo row off and\n   use 15 steps, CFG 2.5.\n4. (muted) One file: the style + the full turbo (rank 68), then a rank-32 copy (126 MB), about 3.3 s.\n\nMeasured (tools/RESULTS.md), four prompts, distance in seeds (1.0 = as different as another seed):\n  surgery -0.30 against the original style LoRA: 0.17 at 15 steps, 0.17 at 8 steps with the turbo\n  (-0.5: 0.46 and 0.38; without surgery 0.55). Row order alone moves 0.12.\n  one file against the two rows live 0.28 (bf16 factors move details at 8 steps), rank 32 against it 0.16.\n\nThe Extractor, Merger and Resize save in models/loras; the Merger takes negative weights (-2 to 2)."
   ],
   "properties": {}
  }
